//! English client digit templates: learned from the eight English sample games of 2026-11-07 (home/vorax
//! 2026-11-07_11-35-12 to 15-47-37), the glyphs cut as for the Traditional Chinese templates ([`super::templates`])
//! and labelled by Windows OCR of the same places (a tank label only where its "a x b" multiplied out to the total
//! read). The English client draws its digits in another face (its 1 has a foot, its 5, 6, 4 and 8 differ), so the
//! Traditional Chinese templates misread them. Feature `en-vorax`, on by default since 1.1.0.
//!
//! Learned by the ignored tests of `read_en.rs`'s `learn` module, which say how to run them: `learn_templates` writes
//! every field, then `round_templates` gives the round's big digits, which replace the ones learned. Every field is
//! learned from its own glyphs but the reward (pooled with the panel's, which have the "9" its own lack): the round and
//! result value of 1.1.0 pooled the panel's digits too, and missed a lossless round 5 and result screen (2026-11-08).
//! The reroll digits are as learned before that change (one "2" fewer, no cell more than 2 off). Learn them again that
//! way rather than editing by hand.

use super::digits::Template;

